# Build output — regenerated by `npm run build`, never edited by hand.
lib/

# Dependencies (the package declares zero runtime dependencies, but npm may
# still create this directory).
node_modules/

# Local scratch: probe scripts and measurement output. The plugin's claims are
# checkable from the source comments and the test suite; anything under
# `.scratch/` is a one-off measurement, not an input to the build.
.scratch/

# Trial-run reports: an agent driving this plugin against one idea writes a long
# Markdown report beside the code. That is an output of USING the plugin, not an
# input to it — the plugin itself never writes inside the workspace (its only
# write is the cache file under `$DSH_HOME/cache/dsh-find-ideas`, see
# `src/cache.ts`). Kept out of the repository so a trial run cannot end up in a
# commit, in the published package, or on GitHub.
*报告.md

# EXCEPTION: the A/B experiment reports are not trial-run output. They are the
# human-readable half of a frozen baseline whose machine-readable half is
# checked in under `eval/runs/ab-v04*-baseline/`, and `eval/harness/ab-wall-clock.mjs`
# READS `v0.4.0-AB实验报告.md` to verify the retracted wall-clock claim still
# appears as a retraction. With the blanket rule above that file is absent from a
# fresh clone and the gate silently degrades to SKIP — a check that cannot run is
# how the retracted column survived a 28-item green gate the first time.
# Committed deliberately; see the commit that added this exception.
!v0.4.0-AB实验报告.md
!v0.4.1-AB实验报告.md

# Archify run receipts under `docs/`: these record the machine that ran the
# render — absolute paths under the user's home directory and the local node
# binary — which is not information the repository should carry. The diagram
# itself is tracked (`docs/dsh-find-ideas.html`, the PNG, and the candidate it
# was built from); re-running `archify finalize` regenerates these receipts on
# any machine, so nothing is lost by leaving them out.
docs/*.finalize.json
docs/*.finalize-summary.json
docs/*.browser-check.json
docs/*.delivery.json

# Local editor / OS state.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The golden harness writes the baseline it is about to overwrite here
# (`--write --force` keeps the old file beside the new one). It is a one-off
# backup of a file that is itself tracked, so committing it would add a second
# copy of the same 90KB on every intentional re-record.
eval/fixtures/inspect-golden-baseline.prev.json

# Tarballs produced by `npm pack` while checking what would be published.
*.tgz
